    "lawCode": "Amd Part E §2, Chap 417 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7623\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend part E of chapter 417 of the laws of 2021 relating to\nauthorizing political subdivisions to permit any public body to hold\nmeetings remotely and without in-person access during the COVID-19 state\ndisaster emergency, in relation to the effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend modifications made to the Open Meetings Law in response to the\nongoing COVID-19 pandemic.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends part E of chapter 417 of the laws of 2021 to allow\npublic bodies to meet remotely by conference call or similar service, so\nlong as the public has the ability to view or listen to such proceeding,\nand provided such meetings are recorded and later transcribed.\n\nSection 2 authorizes the act to take effect immediately and expire on\nApril 1, 2022.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn September of 2021, part E of chapter 417 was enacted to allow public\nbodies to conduct business through videoconferencing without requiring\nin-person public access so long as the general public has the ability to\nview or listen to such proceeding and provided that such meetings are\nrecorded and later transcribed. This legislation extended measures taken\nduring the state disaster emergency and has an expiry date of January\n15, 2022.\n\nAs New York State continues its response to the COVID-19 pandemic, it is\nnecessary to permit local bodies to continue its business while protect-\ning public health. This legislation will extend the current provisions\nfor remote public meetings to continue through April 1, 2022.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nExtends Part E of Chapter 417 of the Laws of 2021.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately.\n",
