    "lawCode": "Amd Part E §§1 & 2, Chap 417 of 2021",
    "lawSection": "Public Officers",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7623A\n\nSPONSOR: GAUGHRAN\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 417 of the laws of 2021 relating to authorizing\npolitical subdivisions to permit any public body to hold meetings\nremotely and without in-person access during the COVID-19 state disaster\nemergency, in relation to public bodies holding meetings remotely and to\nthe effectiveness thereof\n\n \nPURPOSE:\n\nTo extend modifications made to the Open Meetings Law in response to the\nongoing COVID-19 pandemic.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 amends part E of chapter 417 of the laws of 2021 to allow\npublic bodies to meet remotely by conference call or similar service, so\nlong as the public has the ability to view or listen to such proceeding,\nand provided such meetings are recorded and later transcribed.\n\nSection 2 authorizes the act to take effect immediately and expires upon\nthe expiration or termination of the state. disaster emergency declared\npursuant to executive order 11 of 2021 or any extension or modification\nthereof\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nIn September of 2021, part E of chapter 417 was enacted to allow public\nbodies to conduct business through video conferencing without requiring\nin-person public access so long as the general public has the ability to\nview or listen to such proceeding and provided that such meetings are\nrecorded and later transcribed. This legislation extended measures taken\nduring the state disaster emergency and has an expiry date of January\n15, 2022.\n\nAs New York State continues its response to the COVID-19 pandemic, it is\nnecessary to permit local bodies to continue its business while protect-\ning public health. In November 26, 2021 Governor Hochul announced a new\ncovid-19 state disaster emergency due to the increase in cases because\nof new variants of the virus with Executive Order (EO) 11. In December\n26 she extended this EO and granted the legislature the same ability to\nmeet remotely.\n\nThis legislation will extend the current provisions for remote public\nmeetings to continue through the end of the new covid-19 state disaster\nemergency, as well as extend the authorization to all public bodies.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nExtends Part E of Chapter 417 of the Laws of 2021.\n\n \nBUDGET IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nImmediately and shall expire and be deemed repealed upon the expiration\nor termination of the state disaster emergency declared pursuant to\nexecutive order 11 of 2021 or any extension or modification thereof:\nprovided that the commissioner of health shall notify the legislative\nbill drafting commission upon the occurrence of the expiration or termi-\nnation of such executive order in order that the commission may maintain\nan accurate and timely effective database of the official text of the\nlaws of the state of New York in furtherance of effectuating the\nprovisions of section 44 of the legislative law and section 70-b of the\npublic officers law.\n",
